1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,780
Profiles: combining
places and access levels.

2
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:09,426
Use the second and third grant rows
to combine places, mix access levels,

3
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:14,853
control child jurisdictions, and
choose where new records belong.

4
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:19,270
A profile can hold more than one place.

5
00:00:19,270 --> 00:00:23,807
Select the profile box in the
header to open My profiles.

6
00:00:24,173 --> 00:00:29,130
Choose Create a profile to see how
the three grant rows work together.

7
00:00:29,492 --> 00:00:34,068
Under Grants, MERIT gives you
three rows of Place, Role, Access,

8
00:00:34,068 --> 00:00:37,329
and Include everything under this place.

9
00:00:37,687 --> 00:00:42,757
First, make a profile for state-level
work in Maryland and Delaware,

10
00:00:42,757 --> 00:00:45,245
and add a short description.

11
00:00:48,925 --> 00:00:53,820
In the first row, choose Maryland
for Place, Supervisor for Role,

12
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:57,609
and Read and write
without delete for Access.

13
00:00:57,962 --> 00:01:03,485
Clear Include everything under this place
on Maryland, so county agencies like

14
00:01:03,485 --> 00:01:05,868
Harford County are left out.

15
00:01:06,228 --> 00:01:11,382
In the second row, choose Delaware, keep
Supervisor and Read and write without

16
00:01:11,382 --> 00:01:14,227
delete, and keep everything under it.

17
00:01:14,588 --> 00:01:19,534
Leave the third Place on none to
skip it, then choose Save profile.

18
00:01:19,886 --> 00:01:24,677
Next, create a tri-state profile
that uses all three Place rows,

19
00:01:24,677 --> 00:01:27,397
each with its own access level.

20
00:01:34,893 --> 00:01:39,348
In the first row, choose West
Virginia, keep the Supervisor role,

21
00:01:39,348 --> 00:01:41,325
and set Access to Full.

22
00:01:41,911 --> 00:01:48,090
In the second row, choose Virginia,
Supervisor, and Read and write without

23
00:01:48,090 --> 00:01:49,136
delete.

24
00:01:49,436 --> 00:01:53,562
In the third row, choose Pennsylvania,
Supervisor, and Read only,

25
00:01:53,562 --> 00:01:57,644
so you can check neighbouring
cases without changing them.

26
00:01:58,007 --> 00:02:00,712
Save the three-state profile.

27
00:02:01,066 --> 00:02:06,207
Third, use all three rows to read
the whole region, write in Maryland,

28
00:02:06,207 --> 00:02:09,471
and have full access in Harford County.

29
00:02:09,837 --> 00:02:13,912
Set the first row to EPA
Region 3 with Read only access,

30
00:02:13,912 --> 00:02:16,350
keeping everything under it.

31
00:02:16,723 --> 00:02:21,352
Set the second row to Maryland
with Read and write without delete,

32
00:02:21,352 --> 00:02:24,978
and clear Include
everything under this place.

33
00:02:25,330 --> 00:02:31,379
Set the third row to Harford County Health
Department with Full access, and save.

34
00:02:33,733 --> 00:02:38,431
My profiles lists each profile
and every grant row inside it,

35
00:02:38,431 --> 00:02:42,220
including whether child
places are included.

36
00:02:42,584 --> 00:02:45,501
Switch to Maryland state and Delaware.

37
00:02:45,501 --> 00:02:51,274
Work queues shows the two state
tasks, while Harford County stays out.

38
00:02:51,633 --> 00:02:57,419
Switch to West Virginia, Virginia and
Pennsylvania, and Work queues shows the

39
00:02:57,419 --> 00:03:00,073
three tasks from those states.

40
00:03:00,427 --> 00:03:02,743
Switch to the layered profile.

41
00:03:02,743 --> 00:03:08,765
All eight regional tasks appear, and
Intake stays in the menu because Maryland

42
00:03:08,765 --> 00:03:11,172
and Harford allow writing.

43
00:03:11,527 --> 00:03:16,855
When a profile covers several places, use
Working in on My profiles to pick where

44
00:03:16,855 --> 00:03:18,504
new records belong.

45
00:03:20,385 --> 00:03:25,842
Choose Use beside Master profile whenever
you want to return to your full access.

46
00:03:27,011 --> 00:03:32,587
In this video you combined two places in
one profile and cleared Include everything

47
00:03:32,587 --> 00:03:37,827
under this place to leave out a child
county, used all three grant rows to set

48
00:03:37,827 --> 00:03:42,329
different access levels across
three states, and to layer regional,

49
00:03:42,329 --> 00:03:47,703
state and county access, and switched
between the multi-place profiles and chose

50
00:03:47,703 --> 00:03:49,917
Working in for new records.
